# The archived harness streamed reviews out of a 750 GB public corpus, so its
# reviews.csv was large and reproducible and did not belong in git.
#
# LIVE collection inverts that. A batch read from Amazon on a given day CANNOT
# be re-collected: the page has already changed, the sort was never stable, and
# pagination is dead on that surface. The collected reviews are the only copy
# there will ever be, so they are committed.
#
# scores.csv stays ignored - it IS reproducible, by re-running the scorer over
# the committed reviews.
data/*/reviews_raw.jsonl
data/*/scores.csv
data/*/*/scores.csv
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Refetch cache for the rolling screen; safe to delete, costs only refetch time.
.cache/

# Development/verification venv — numpy and scipy, used only as the oracle the
# in-repo statistics are cross-checked against. Never a pipeline dependency, so
# it is never needed to reproduce a results.jsonl row. Rebuild it from
# requirements-dev.txt; see references/numeric-stack.md.
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets. Never committed — API tokens live here, not in the repo.
.env
.env.*
